.TH XYMONLIVE.CGI 1 "Version 4.3.31" "Xymon"
.SH NAME
xymonlive.cgi \- live browser view of current Xymon statuses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "xymonlive.cgi [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xymonlive.cgi
serves an HTML5 dashboard that polls xymond directly. It does not read the
history or allevents files. The dashboard shows current red, yellow, purple,
and blue statuses, acknowledgement and disabled state, and observed changes
between browser polls.
.PP
The change list is intentionally a sampled browser view, not a durable event
log. A status that changes twice between polls may not appear, and a status
that leaves the non-green set is shown as green.
.PP
With the query parameter
.B data=1
the CGI returns the current status snapshot as JSON. This mode is used by the
dashboard and is not intended as a replacement for the Xymon channel protocol.
.PP
JSON snapshots are cached in XYMONTMP. Concurrent requests share a cached
snapshot, and only one CGI process refreshes it from xymond. During a refresh
or a temporary xymond failure, an existing stale snapshot remains available.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\fB\-\-env=FILENAME\fR"
Load the Xymon environment from FILENAME.
.IP "\fB\-\-area=NAME\fR"
Load environment settings for the named area.
.IP "\fB\-\-cache=SECONDS\fR"
Cache JSON snapshots for this many seconds. The default is 3 seconds. Set this
to 0 to disable caching.
.IP "\fB\-\-debug\fR"
Enable debugging output.
.SH SEE ALSO
xymon(1), xymond(8), appfeed.cgi(1)